  steps:
    1. Set grid 30x30, bg=0. Pick one clutter color from {1,2,4,5,6,7,8,9}.
    2. Build corridor cross (the output green region):
       a. Choose V-bar column range (true width 4-10, positioned so bar interior >= 2 wide).
          Span full height or 80%+ of grid rows, touching at least one vertical edge.
       b. Choose H-bar row range (true height 4-12) intersecting the V-bar.
          Extend from V-bar to at least one horizontal grid edge. Optionally split
          into 2 segments separated by a gap.
       c. Mark the cross interior (true region minus 1px margin) as green = output corridor.
    3. Fill non-corridor region with clutter:
       Mark each pixel outside the cross (including margin) as clutter with probability 0.45-0.50,
       otherwise leave as bg. Ensure NO clutter inside the cross or its 1px margin.
    4. Derive input from output: replace all green pixels with bg (0).
    5. Validate: run solver on input and verify output matches.
